"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Raff Ciccone","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10915","person_slug":"raff-ciccone","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ralph Babet","party":"United Australia Party","person_id":"tvfy_11003","person_slug":"ralph-babet","vote":"no"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"no"},{"name":"Richard Dowling","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11056","person_slug":"richard-dowling","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ross Cadell","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_11004","person_slug":"ross-cadell","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sarah Henderson","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10790","person_slug":"sarah-henderson","vote":"no"},{"name":"Slade Brockman","party":"DPRES","person_id":"tvfy_10900","person_slug":"slade-brockman","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steph Hodgins-May","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_11020","person_slug":"steph-hodgins-may","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Susan McDonald","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10951","person_slug":"susan-mcdonald","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tim Ayres","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10946","person_slug":"tim-ayres","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tyron Whitten","party":"One Nation","person_id":"tvfy_11060","person_slug":"tyron-whitten","vote":"no"},{"name":"Varun Ghosh","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_11017","person_slug":"varun-ghosh","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Wendy Askew","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10914","person_slug":"wendy-askew","vote":"no"}],"name":"Motions - Australia: Racism - Reject and condemn","noes":28,"question":"The majority voted in favour of the [motion](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2025-09-01.91.2) introduced by NSW Senator [Jenny McAllister](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/nsw/jenny_mcallister) (Labor) and amended by ACT Senator [Katy Gallagher](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/act/katy_gallagher) (Labor), which means it was successful. These types of motions do not make any legal changes on their own but are politically influential because they represent the will of the Senate. ### Amendment text > *That the Senate* > > *(a) affirms that Australia is a nation that welcomes different races, religions and views, united by respect for each other's humanity and for each other's right to live in peace;* > > *(b) therefore rejects the racism, white supremacy and condemnation of immigrants on display at rallies held over the weekend, and profoundly disapproves of MPs supporting and attending these rallies;* > > *(c) condemns the far-right extremist neo-Nazis, including the National Socialist Network, who in Melbourne attacked Camp Sovereignty, a site of Aboriginal resistance and sacred resting place of 38 Nations;* > > *(d) calls upon all political representatives to:* > >> *(i) reject the normalisation or legitimisation of racism and anti-immigrant hate in this country,* >> >> *(ii) reject dog whistling on First Peoples, migrants, refugees and international students, which has emboldened the far right,* >> >> *(iii) reject any use of hate, fear and scapegoating to cover up their own policy failures on the housing and cost of living crises,* >> >> *(iv) reject any attempt to downplay or ignore concerns about far-right extremism, and* >> >> *(v) stand together against far-right extremism as alien to Australia and the values of this nation; and* > > *(e) reiterates its solidarity with the communities who bear the brunt of white supremacy, neo-Nazism and right-wing extremism.*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-9737","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2025-09-01/12"}
